hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1580","I said: I will. Then I too fell asleep. I woke up when the sun had already risen. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) also woke up upon hearing our conversation. Then he instructed Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him). He gave the adhan, then he gave the iqamah, and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) led us in prayer."
"1581","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Whoever catches one rak'ah before the sun rises and then the sun rises, he should complete the second rak'ah with it."
"1582","If anyone says a rak'ah of the 'Asr prayer before sunset, he has observed (the 'Asr prayer), and if anyone performs a rak'ah of the Fajr prayer, he has observed (the Fajr prayer). (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 412)"
"1583","narrates this statement of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: ""Whoever catches one rak'ah of the Fajr prayer before sunrise has caught the Fajr prayer, and whoever catches one rak'ah of the Asr prayer before sunset has caught the Asr prayer."
"1584","The Messenger of Allah said: ""Whoever catches one Rak'ah of the 'Asr before the sun sets, then he has caught it, and whoever catches one Rak'ah of the Subh before the sun rises, then he has caught it."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 699)"
"1585","If anyone says a rak'ah of the 'Asr prayer before sunset, he has observed (the 'Asr prayer), and if anyone performs a rak'ah of the Fajr prayer, he has observed (the Fajr prayer). (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 412)"
"1586","""If any one of you catches the first prostration of 'Asr prayer before the sun sets, let him complete his prayer, and if he catches up with the first prostration of Fajr prayer before the sub rises, let him complete his prayer."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 516)"
"1587","""When the dawn appears, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would only pray two short Rak'ahs."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 583)"
"1588","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to perform two rak‘ahs before Maghrib. Then he said: ""You people should also perform two rak‘ahs before Maghrib."" Then, for the third time, he said: (This command is for the one) who wishes to perform these two rak‘ahs. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) feared that people might consider it as a Sunnah."
"1589","""When the Mu'adhdhin called the Adhan, some of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ would get up and rush to the pillars (in the Masjid) and pray until the Prophet ﷺ came out and they were like that. They would pray before Maghrib and there was nothing between the Adhan and Iqamah."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 682)"
"1590","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) performed the Zuhr and Asr prayers together, and the Maghrib and Isha prayers together during a journey."
"1591","I asked, ""Why did the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) do this?"" So Sayyiduna Mu'adh replied: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) wanted that he should not put his Ummah in difficulty."
"1592","""If the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was setting out on a journey before the sun passed its zenith, he would delay Zuhr until the time of 'Asr, then he would stop and combine the prayer. If the sun passed its zenith before he set out, he would pray Zuhr and then set off. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 586)"
"1593","The Prophet ﷺ was engaged in the Battle of Tabuk. If he moved off before the sun had declined, he would delay the noon prayer till he would combine it with the afternoon prayer and would offer them together. If he moved off after the sun had declined, he would combine the noon and afternoon prayers, and then he proceeded; if he moved off before the evening prayer, he would delay the evening prayer; he would offer it along with the night prayer, he would delay the evening prayer; he would offer it along with the night prayer. If he moved off after the evening prayer, he would offer the night prayer earlier and offer it along with the evening prayer. Abu Dawud said: This tradition has not been narrated by anyone except by Qutaibah. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1220)"
"1594","The Apostle of Allaah ﷺ returned from ‘Arafah. When he came to the mountain path , he alighted, urinated and performed the ablution, but he did not perform it completely. I said to him Prayer? He said “The prayer will be offered ahead of you.” He then mounted. When he reached Al Muzdalifah he alighted performed the ablution, performed it well. Thereafter iqamah for the prayer was called and he offered the sunset prayer. Then everyone made his Camel kneel down at his place. Iqamah was then called for night prayer and he offered it but he did not pray between them. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1925)"
"1595","God willing, you would reach by tomorrow the fountain of Tabuk and you should not come to that until it is dawn, and he who amongst you happens to go there should not touch its water until I come. We came to that and two persons (amongst) us reached that fountain ahead of us. It was a thin flow of water like the shoelace. Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked them whether they had touched the water. They said: Yes. Allah's Apostle ﷺ scolded them, and he said to them what he had to say by the will of God. The people then took water of the fountain in their palms until it became somewhat significant and Messenger of Allah ﷺ washed his hands and his face too in it, and then, took it again in that (fountain) and there gushed forth abundant water from that fountain, until all the people drank to their fill. He then said: Mu'adh, it is likely that if you live long that you see what is here filled with gardens. (Using translation from Muslim 706c)"
"1596","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Zuhr and 'Asr together, and Maghrib and 'Isha' together, when there was no fear and he was not traveling."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 601)"
"1597","Ibn 'Abbas reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ observed in Medina seven (rak'ahs) and eight (rak'ahs), i. e. (be combined) the noon and afternoon prayers (eight rak'ahs) and the sunset and 'Isha' prayers (seven rak'ahs). (Using translation from Muslim 705f)"
"1598","""I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Which mosque was built first?' He said: 'Al-Masjid Al-Haram (in Makkah).' I said: 'Then which?' He said: 'then Al-Masjid Al-Aqsa (in Jerusalem).' I said: 'How many years between them?' He said: 'Forty years, but the whole earth is a mosque for you, so pray wherever you are when the time for prayer comes.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 753)"
"1599","I do not know; I will ask Jibreel about this."" Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) asked Jibreel (peace be upon him), and he replied, ""I do not know; I will ask Mikaeel about this."" Then he came and informed: ""The best part of the earth is the mosques, and the worst part is the markets."
"1600","The parts of land dearest to Allah are its mosques, and the parts most hateful to Allah are markets. (Using translation from Muslim 671)"
"1601","In the lifetime of Messenger of Allah ﷺ the mosque was built of adobes, its roof of the leaves of date-palms and its pillars of the stems of date-palms. Abu Bakr did not alter it. ʿUmar expanded it on the same pattern as it was in the lifetime of Messenger of Allah ﷺ by using adobes, leaves of date-palms and changing the pillars into wooden ones. ʿUthman changed it by expanding it to a great extent and built its walls with engraved stones and lime and made its pillars of engraved stones and its roof of teak wood. (Using translation from Bukhārī 446)"
"1602","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Keep adding more water to it, for as a result, its purity will only increase. The narrator says: We set out, and we disagreed about who would carry the vessel of water, so the Prophet (peace be upon him) assigned each of us a turn for one day and one night. We took it with us until we reached our area, and then we did as the Prophet (peace be upon him) had commanded us. The priest of that people was a man from the tribe of Tay. When we gave the call to prayer, the priest said: This is the call of truth. Then he ran away and was never seen again."
"1603","The narrator says the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) did so, and then he fell to the ground. His eyes turned towards the sky, then he stood up and said: ""My waistcloth, my waistcloth."" Then he tied his waistcloth around himself."
"1604","The other said that it refers to Masjid Quba. They both came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), so he said: ""It refers to this mosque of mine."
"1605","narrates: There was a disagreement between two men regarding the mosque which was founded on piety. One of them said that (by this) is meant the mosque of Madinah Munawwarah (i.e., Masjid Nabawi), and the other said it is Masjid Quba. They both came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), so he said: “By this is meant this mosque of mine.”"
"1606","""Two men argued about the Masjid which was founded on piety from the first day. [1] One man said that it was the Masjid of Quba', and the other said that it was the Masjid of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'It is this Masjid of mine.'"" [1] At-Tawbah 9:108. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 697)"
"1607","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him: \""Whoever makes the mosque his home for performing prayer or for the remembrance of Allah (i.e., he stays there), then Allah is as pleased with that person as the family of a person who was absent is pleased upon his return.\"" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) When the Arabs intend to describe a quality by way of analogy between two different things,"
"1608","""I heard the Messenger of Allah say: 'Whoever builds a mosque in which the Name of Allah is mentioned, Allah will build a house for him in Paradise.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 735)"
"1609","The narrator named Bukair says: I think these words are also in the narration: ""(builds a mosque) for the sake of attaining Allah Almighty's pleasure."
"1610","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever builds a mosque for the sake of Allah (from his own wealth), Allah will build a house for him in Paradise.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 737)"
"1611","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Whoever builds a mosque for the sake of Allah's pleasure, even if it is as small as a bird's nest, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise."
"1612","""Sometimes it is dark or rainy or there is a flood, and I am a blind man; 0 Messenger of Allah ﷺ, (come and) pray in a place in my house that I may take as a prayer-place."" He said: ""Where would you like me to pray for you?"" He showed him a place in his house, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed there. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 788)"
"1613","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade that people build mosques in order to boast against one another."
"1614","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until people boast to one another regarding the"
"1615","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have not been commanded to adorn the mosques."" Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: ""You people will adorn these mosques just as the Jews and Christians adorned (their places of worship)."" The narrator Abu Fazarah is Rashid bin Kaysan, and he is among the trustworthy and reliable narrators from Kufa."
"1616","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Indeed, of the places to which one travels mounted, the best are this mosque of mine (i.e., the Prophet's Mosque) and Bayt 'Ateeq (i.e., the Sacred Mosque)."
"1617","Messenger of Allah said: ""A mount is not saddled (for a journey) except to three Masajid: Al-Masjid Al-Haram, this Masjid of mine, and Masjid Al-Aqsa."" [Abu ʿEisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih. (Using translation from Tirmidhī 326)"
"1618","The Prophet ﷺ used to go to the Quba' mosque, sometimes walking, sometimes riding. (Using translation from Bukhārī 7326)"
"1619","“No one should prepare a mount (travel) to visit any mosque except three: the Sacred Mosque, this mosque of mine, and Aqsa Mosque.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1409)"
"1620","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Offering one prayer in this mosque of mine is more virtuous than offering a thousand prayers anywhere else, except for Al-Masjid Al-Haram. In Al-Masjid Al-Haram, offering one prayer is more virtuous than offering one hundred prayers here.\"" (The narrator says) This refers to the mosque of Madinah Munawwarah."""""
"1621","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Performing one prayer in the mosque of Allah’s Messenger is more virtuous than performing one thousand prayers anywhere else, except for Masjid al-Haram. The reason for this is that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) is the last Prophet and his mosque is the last mosque (i.e., that will be attributed to any Prophet). The narrators named Abu Salamah and Abu Abdullah state: We have no doubt about this matter; Sayyiduna Abu Hu"
"1622","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whoever leaves his house heading towards this mosque of mine, for every step he takes, a good deed is written for him, and with the next step, one of his sins is erased. (This continues) until he returns."
"1623","I want to go to Bayt al-Maqdis."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Offering one prayer in this mosque (i.e., the Prophet's Mosque) is more virtuous than offering one hundred prayers anywhere else, except for al-Masjid al-Haram, which is different."
"1624","I intend to go to Bayt al-Maqdis."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Offering one prayer in this mosque (i.e., Masjid Nabawi) is more virtuous than offering one hundred prayers anywhere else, except for Masjid al-Haram, which is a different matter."" The narrator named Uthman bin Abu Shaybah says: Imam Ahmad bin Hanbal asked me about this narration."
"1625","Messenger of Allah said: ""Salat is this Masjid of mine is better than a thousand Salat in another, except for Masjid Al-Haram."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 325)"
"1626","The Khudri man said: It refers to the mosque of the Prophet (peace be upon him). The Amri man said: It refers to the mosque of Quba. The narrator states: Both of them went out and presented themselves before the Prophet (peace be upon him) and asked him about this matter. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: It refers to this mosque, it refers to the mosque of Allah’s Messenger, and there is much goodness in it."
"1627","I am going to that mosque which is in the neighborhood of Banu Amr bin Awf, because I heard the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, say: ‘Whoever offers prayer in it, it is equal to performing an ‘Umrah.’”"
"1628","Ibn Umar reported that Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited (the mosque) at Quba' riding and on foot. (Using translation from Muslim 1399a)"
"1629","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to go to the Quba Mosque either riding or walking."
"1630","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to come to Quba walking and riding."
"1631","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A journey should be undertaken only towards three mosques: Al-Masjid Al-Haram, this mosque of mine, and the mosque of Al-Aqsa (i.e., Bayt Al-Maqdis)."
"1632","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to come to Quba every week on a specific day."
"1633","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I hope that Allah Almighty also granted him this third thing."
"1634","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to build mosques in different localities (i.e. in the locality of each tribe separately) and that they should be kept clean and be perfumed. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 455)"
"1635","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Spitting in the mosque is a sin and it is expiated by burying the spittle. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 475)"
"1636","A man led the people in prayer. He spat towards qiblah while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was looking at him. The Messenger of Allah said to the people when he finished his prayer: He should not lead you in prayer (henceforth). Thenceforth he intended to lead them in prayer, but they forbade him and informed him of the prohibition of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who said to him: Yes. The narrator said: I think he (the Prophet) said: You did harm to Allah and His Apostle. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 481)"
"1637","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Spitting in the mosque is a sin and it is expiated by burying the spittle. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 475)"
"1638","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “A person who spits in the direction of the qiblah (in the mosque), when he comes on the Day of Resurrection, that spit will be stuck to his face.”"
"1639","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever spits in the direction of the Qiblah, when he comes on the Day of Resurrection, his spit will be between his two eyes."
"1640","""My nation was shown to me with their good deeds and bad deeds. Among their good deeds I saw a harmful thing being removed from the road. And among their bad deeds I saw sputum in the mosque that had not been removed."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3683)"
"1641","The Apostle of Allah ﷺ said: The deeds of my people, good and bad, were presented before me, and I found the removal of something objectionable from the road among their good deeds, and the sputum mucus left unburied in the mosque among their evil deeds. (Using translation from Muslim 553)"
"1642","I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: A human being has three hundred and sixty joints for each of which he must give alms. The people asked him: Who is capable of doing this ? He replied: It may be mucus in the mosque which you bury, and something which you remove from the road; but if you do not find such, two rak'ahs in the forenoon will be sufficient for you. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5242)"
"1643","Zirr ibn Hubaysh said: Hudhayfah traced, I think, to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the saying: He who spits in the direction of the qiblah will come on the Day of Resurrection in the state that his saliva will be between his eyes; and he who eats from this noxious vegetable should not come near our mosque, saying it three times. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3824)"
"1644","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \""Whoever eats this vegetable, meaning garlic, onion, or leek, should not come to our mosques, because the angels are bothered by that which bothers humans.\"""""""
"1645","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""Whoever eats from this tree should by no means cause us discomfort in our gatherings.\"" By this, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) meant garlic."""""
"1646","I not forbid you from this foul vegetable (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words) — this odorous vegetable? Whoever eats it should not come to our mosques, because the angels are harmed by that which harms human beings."
"1647","narrate that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said to a person passing through the mosque with an arrow: 'Hold it by its pointed end'?"" He replied, ""Yes."
"1648","Jabir said “The Apostle of Allaah ﷺ ordered a man who was distributing arrows not to pass the mosque with them except that he is holding their heads. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2586)"
"1649","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a person passes through our marketplace or mosque carrying arrows, he should hold them by their tips so that they do not harm any Muslim."
"1650","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you see someone buying and selling in the mosque, say: May Allah not grant profit in your trade."
"1651","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \""Whoever hears someone announcing a lost item in the mosque, let him say: May Allah not return it to you, for the mosques were not built for this purpose.\"""""""
"1652","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) had finished the prayer when a man said: Who will guide me to the red camel? The Pro"
"1653","Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) passed by Sayyiduna Hassan bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) when he was reciting poet"
"1654","I see you in separate groups?"
"1655","I was standing with them when the kite flew by and dropped the necklace, which fell among them. The slave girl says: I said, ""Here is the thing for which you accused me. You people thought so, but I was innocent of it. Here is the necklace."" The slave girl narrates: Then she went to the service of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) and accepted Islam. Lady Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: A tent was set up for this slave girl in the mosque. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The slave girl used to come to me and talk with me. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says: Whenever she came and sat with me, she would recite this verse: ""The day of the necklace was one of the wondrous signs of my Lord; surely He saved me from the land of disbelief."" Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says: I asked the slave girl, ""What is the reason that whenever you come and sit with me, you recite this verse?"" Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Then the slave girl told me the whole incident."
"1656","I used to sleep in the mosque in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when I was young and bachelor. The dogs would urinate frequently visit the mosque, and no one would sprinkle over it. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 382)"
"1657","“At the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ we used to eat bread and meat in the mosque.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3300)"
"1658","""We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and we were young men close in age. He let us stay with him for twenty days. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was merciful and compassionate, and he thought that we were missing our families; he asked us about those whom we had left behind of our families, so we told him, and he said: 'Go back to your families, stay with them and teach them. Tell them when the time for prayer comes; let one of you call the Adhan and let the oldest of you lead the prayer.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 635)"
"1659","""If the people knew what (virtue) there was in the call to prayer and the first row, and they not find any way to get to do that [1] other than by drawing lots, they would do that. If they knew what (virtue) there was in coming early to prayer, they would compete to be first in the Masjid. If they knew what (virtue) there was in Al-'Atamah and Subh, they would come to them even if they had to crawl."" [1] Indicating the two mentioned items: that is the call to prayer and praying in the first row. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 540)"
"1660","""I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Your Lord is pleased with a shepherd high in the mountains who calls the Adhan for the prayer and prays. Allah says: 'Look at this slave of Mine; he calls the Adhan and Iqamah for the prayer and fears Me. I have forgiven My slave and admitted him to Paradise.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 666)"
"1661","I have seen that you like to live among sheep and goats and prefer a rural life (the narrator is in doubt, or perhaps these are the words), or you live among sheep and goats and in the wilderness. So, give the call to prayer (adhan) and raise your voice while giving the adhan, for wherever the voice of the muezzin reaches, whatever jinn, human, or anything else hears it, it will bear witness in favor of that muezzin on the Day of Resurrection."" Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say this."
"1662","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the muezzin gives the call to prayer (adhan), Satan turns his back and goes away, passing wind. When the muezzin becomes silent, he returns. Then when the muezzin gives the iqamah, he again turns his back and goes away, passing wind. When the muezzin becomes silent, Satan comes back and begins to cast different thoughts into a person's heart, to the extent that a person does not even remember how many units of prayer he has performed. When someone faces such a situation while praying, he should perform two prostrations of forgetfulness (sajda sahw) during the sitting (qa'dah)."
"1663","Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""When the Adhan is pronounced Satan takes to his heels and passes wind with noise during his flight in order not to hear the Adhan. When the Adhan is completed he comes back and again takes to his heels when the Iqama is pronounced and after its completion he returns again till he whispers into the heart of the person (to divert his attention from his prayer) and makes him remember things which he does not recall to his mind before the prayer and that causes him to forget how much he has prayed."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 608)"
"1664","When Satan hears the call to prayer, he runs away to a distance like that of Rauha. Sulaimin said: I asked him about Rauha. He replied: It is at a distance of thirty-six miles from Medina. (Using translation from Muslim 388a)"
"1665","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) heard a man during a journey who was saying « » « » (i.e., he was giving the call to prayer). The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is upon the natural disposition (fitrah)."" Then he said: « » , so the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hellfire has become forbidden for him."" We hurried to this man and found that he was a shepherd of animals, and when the time for prayer came, he was giving the call to prayer for it."
"1666","The Prophet ﷺ said: The mu'adhdhin will receive forgiveness to the extent to which his voice reaches, and every moist and dry place will testify on his behalf; and he who attends (the congregation of) prayer will have twenty-five prayers recorded for him and will have expiation for sins committed between every two times of prayer. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 515)"
"1667","""We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Bilal stood up and gave the call. When he fell silent the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever says the same as this (what the Mu'adhdhin) with certainty, he will enter Paradise. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 674)"
"1668","A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: My riding beast has been killed, so give me some animal to ride upon. He (the Holy Prophet) said: I have none with me. A man said: Messenger of Allah, I can guide him to one who will provide him with a riding beast. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: One who guides to something good has a reward similar to that of its doer. (Using translation from Muslim 1893a)"
"1669","""I heard Mu'awiyah bin Abu Sufyan say that Messenger of Allah said: ""The Mu'adh-dhin will have the longest necks of all people on the Day of Resurrection."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 725)"
"1670","""I heard Mu'awiyah bin Abu Sufyan say that Messenger of Allah said: ""The Mu'adh-dhin will have the longest necks of all people on the Day of Resurrection."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 725)"
"1671","The imam is responsible and the mu'adhdhin is trusted, O Allah, guide the imams and forgive the mu'adhdhins. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 517)"
"1672","The imam is responsible and the mu'adhdhin is trusted, O Allah, guide the imams and forgive the mu'adhdhins. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 517)"
"1673","Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), and Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), the words of the adhan were said twice (that is, on the day of Jumu'ah there was one adhan and one iqamah), until the era of Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) came and the people increased in number, so he instructed the mu'adhdhin to give a second adhan at the place of Zawra' (on the day of Jumu'ah)."
"1674","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: In the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the words of the adhan were said twice and the iqamah was said once, however, «قد قامت الصلوۃ» was said twice. When we heard the iqamah, we would perform ablution and come for the prayer."""""
"1675","Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) was commanded to say the words of the adhan in even numbers and the words of the iqamah in odd"
"1676","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Bilal to say the phrases of the Adhan twice and the phrases of the Iqamah once."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 627)"
"1677","The narrator named Abu Ja’far was the imam of the Ansar’s mosque in Kufa; his name is Muhammad bin Muslim bin Mihran bin Muthanna, while the narrator named Abu Muthanna’s name is Muslim bin Muthanna."
"1678","""They looked for something by means of which they could call out informing of (the time of) the prayer. Then Bilal was commanded to say the phrases of the Adhan twice and the phrases of the Iqamah once."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 729)"
"1679","when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered a bell to be made so that it might be struck to gather the people for prayer, a man carrying a bell in his hand appeared to me while I was asleep, and I said; servant of ‘abd Allah, will you sell the bell? He asked; what will you do with it? I replied; we shall use it to call the people to prayer. He said; should I not suggest you something better than that. I replied: certainly. Then he told me to say: Allah is most great, Allah is most great, Allah is most great, Allah is most great. I testify that there is no god but Allah, I testify that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. Come to pray, come to pray; come to salvation; come to salvation. Allah is most great, Allah is most great. I testify that there is no god but Allah. He then moved backward a few steps and said: when you utter the IQAMAH, you should say: Allah is most great, Allah is most great. I testify that there is no god but Allah, I testify that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. Come to prayer, come to salvation. The time for prayer has come, the time for prayer has come: Allah is most great, Allah is most great. There is no god but Allah. When the morning came, I came to the Messenger of Allah (May peace be upon him) and informed him of what I had seen in the dream. He said: it is a genuine vision, and he then should use it to call people to prayer, for he has a louder voice than you have. So I got up along with Bilal and began to teach it to him and he used it in making the call to prayer. ‘Umar b. al-khattab (Allah be pleased with him) heard it while he was in his house and came out trailing his cloak and said: Messenger of Allah. By him who has sent you with the truth, I have also seen the kind of thing as has been shown to him. The Messenger of Allah (May peace be upon him) said: To Allah be the praise. Abu Dawud said; Al-Zuhri narrated this tradition in a similar way from Sa’id b. al-Musayyib on the authority of ‘Abd Allah b. Zaid. In this version Ibn Ishaq narrated from al-Zuhri: Allah is most great. Allah is most great, Allah is most great, Allah is most great. Ma;mar and yunus narrated from al-Zuhri; Allah is most great, Allah is most great. They did not report it twice again. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 499)"
"1680","""Abdul-'Aziz bin 'Abdul-Malik bin Abu Mahdhurah narrated from 'Abdullah bin muhairiz who was an orphan under the care of Abu Mahdhurah bin mi'yar that when he was preparing him to travel to Sham, he said: 'O my uncle, I am going out to Sham, and I will be asked about how you started the Adhan.' So he informed me that. Abu Mahdhurah said: 'I went out with a group of people, and we were somewhere on the road, when the Mu'adh-dhin of the Messenger of Allah gave the call to prayer in the presence of the Messenger of Allah. We heard the voice of the Mu'adh-dhin, and we were shunning it (the Adhan), so we started yelling, imitating it and mocking it. The Messenger of Allah heard us, so he sent some people who brought us to sit in front of him. He said: 'Who is the one whose voice I heard so loud?' The people all pointed to me, and they were telling the truth. He sent them all away, but kept me there and said to me: 'Stand up and give the call to prayer.' I stood up and there was nothing more hateful to me than the Messenger of Allah and what he was telling me to do. I stood up in front of the Messenger of Allah and the Messenger of Allah himself taught me the call. He said: ""Say: 'Allahu Akbar Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar Allahu Akbar; Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah, Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah; Ash-hadu anna Muhammadan Rasulullah, Ash-hadu anna Muhammadan Rasulullah (Allah is the Most great, Allah is the most Great, Allah is the most Great, Allah is the most Great; I bear witness that none has the right to be worshipped but Allah, I bear witness that none has the right to be worshipped but Allah; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah).'"" Then he said: ""Raise your voice (and say). Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah, Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah; Ash-hadu anna Muhammadan Rasulullah, Ash-hadu anna Muhammadan Rasulullah; Hayya 'alal-salah, Hayya 'alal-salah; Hayya 'alal-falah, Hayya 'alal-falah; Allahu Akbar Allahu Akbar; La ilaha illallah (I bear witness that none has the right to be worshipped but Allah, I bear witness that none has the right to be worshipped but Allah; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; Come to the Prayer, Come to the Prayer; Come to the prosperity, Come to the prosperity; Allah is the Most great, Allah is the Most Great; None has the right to be worshipped but Allah).'"" Then he called me when I had finished saying the Adhan, and gave me a small bag in which there was some silver. Then he put his hand on the forelock of Abu Mahdhurah, then passed it over his face, then over his chest, and over his heart, until the hand of the Messenger of Allah reached his navel. Then the Messenger of Allah said: 'May Allah bless you and send blessings upon you.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, do you command me to give the call to prayer in Makkah?' He said: 'Yes, I command you (to do so).' Then all the hatred I had felt towards the Messenger of Allah disappeared, and was replaced with love for the Messenger of Allah. I came to 'Attab bin Asid, the governor of the Messenger of Allah in Makkah, and gave the call to prayer with him by command of the Messenger of Allah."" (Sahih)He ('Abdul-'Aziz) said: ""Someone who met Abu Mahdhurah told me the same as 'Abdullah bin Muhairiz told me."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 708)"
"1681","""The Messenger of Allah taught me the Adhan with nineteen phrases and the Iqamah with seventeen. The Adhan is: Allahu Akbar Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar Allahu Akbar; Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah, Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah; Ash-hadu anna Muhammadan Rasulullah, Ash-hadu anna Muhammadan Rasulullah; Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah, Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah; Ash-hadu anna Muhammadan Rasulullah, Ash-hadu anna Muhammadan Rasulullah; Hayya 'alal-salah, Hayya 'alal-salah; Hayya 'alal-falah, Hayya 'alal-falah; Allahu Akbar Allahu Akbar; La ilaha illallah (Allah is the Most great, Allah is the most Great, Allah is the most Great, Allah is the most Great; I bear witness that none has the right to be worshipped but Allah, I bear witness that none has the right to be worshipped but Allah; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; I bear witness that none has the right to be worshipped but Allah, I bear witness that none has the right to be worshipped but Allah; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; Come to the Prayer, Come to the Prayer; Come to the prosperity, Come to the prosperity; Allah is the Most great, Allah is the Most Great; None has the right to be worshipped but Allah). And the Iqamah is seventeen phrases: Allahu Akbar Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar Allahu Akbar; Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah, Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah; Ash-hadu anna Muhammadan Rasulullah, Ash-hadu anna Muhammadan Rasulullah; Hayya 'alal-salah, Hayya 'alal-salah; Hayya 'alal-falah, Hayya 'alal-falah; Qad qamatis-salah, qad qamatis-salah; Allahu Akbar Allahu Akbar; La ilaha illallah (Allah is the Most great, Allah is the most Great, Allah is the most Great, Allah is the most Great; I bear witness that none has the right to be worshipped but Allah, I bear witness that none has the right to be worshipped but Allah; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; Come to the Prayer, Come to the Prayer; Come to the prosperity, Come to the prosperity; The prayer is about to begin, the prayer is about to begin; Allah is the Most great, Allah is the Most Great; None has the right to be worshipped but Allah)."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 709)"
"1682","I testify that there is no god but Allah, I testify that there is no god but Allah; I testify that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I testify that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. Lowering your voice while saying them (these words). Then you must raise your voice in making the testimony: I testify that there is no god but Allah, I testify there is no god but Allah; I testify Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I testify Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. Come to prayer, come to prayer; come to salvation, come to salvation. If it is the morning prayer, you must pronounce; prayer is better than sleep, prayer is better than sleep, Allah is most great; there is no god but Allah. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 500)"
"1683","“And I too, and I too”. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 526)"
"1684","I also bear witness to this. When the muezzin said « » , Sayyiduna Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I also bear witness to this. Then Sayyiduna Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) explained: I heard the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) responding to the adhan in this manner."
"1685","“Allah is most great, Allah is most great”, and one of you says in response: “Allah is most great”, Allah is most great; then says: “ I testify tht there is no god but Allah”, and he says in response: “I testify that there is no god but Allah”, then say:” I testify that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah”, and he makes the response: “ I testify that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah”, then says: “Come to prayer”, and he makes the response: “There is no might and no power except in Allah”: then says: “ Allah is most great, Allah is most great”, and he makes the response: “Allah is most great”, then says: “There is no god but Allah”, if he says this from his heart, he enter Paradise. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 527)"
"1686","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you hear the muezzin, say the same words as he says."
"1687","“Allah is most great, Allah is most great”, and one of you says in response: “Allah is most great”, Allah is most great; then says: “ I testify tht there is no god but Allah”, and he says in response: “I testify that there is no god but Allah”, then say:” I testify that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah”, and he makes the response: “ I testify that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah”, then says: “Come to prayer”, and he makes the response: “There is no might and no power except in Allah”: then says: “ Allah is most great, Allah is most great”, and he makes the response: “Allah is most great”, then says: “There is no god but Allah”, if he says this from his heart, he enter Paradise. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 527)"
"1688","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) said the same. The muezzin said « » , so Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) said the same. The muezzin said « » , so Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) said the same. Then he turned to me and said: Sayyiduna Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to me a hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) in this manner."
"1689","if anyone says when he hears the call to prayer : “O Allah, Lord of this perfect call and of the prayer which is established for all time, grant Muhammad the wasilah and excellency, and raise him up in a praiseworthy position which Thou hast promised, he will be assured of my intercession. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 529)"
"1690","when you hear the mu'adhdhin repeat what he says, invoke a blessing on me, for everyone who invoke one blessing on me will receive ten blessings from Allah. Then ask Allah to give me the wasilah, which is a rank in paradise fitting for only one of Allah’s servants, and I hope that I may be the one. If anyone asks Allah that I be given the wasilah, he will be assured of my intercession. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 523)"
"1691","""I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'When you hear the Mu'adhdhin then say what he says, and do Salah upon me, for whoever does Salah upon me once, Allah will Salah upon him ten (times). Then ask Allah to grant me Al-Wasilah, which is a position in paradise which only one of the slaves of Allah will attain, and I hope that I will be the one. Whoever asks for Al-Wasilah for me, will be entitled to my intercession.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 678)"
"1692","when you hear the mu'adhdhin repeat what he says, invoke a blessing on me, for everyone who invoke one blessing on me will receive ten blessings from Allah. Then ask Allah to give me the wasilah, which is a rank in paradise fitting for only one of Allah’s servants, and I hope that I may be the one. If anyone asks Allah that I be given the wasilah, he will be assured of my intercession. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 523)"
"1693","If anyone says when he hears the MU’ADHDHIN : “And I testify that there is no god but Allah alone who has no partner and that Muhammad is His servant and Apostle: I am satisfied with Allah as lord, with Muhammad as apostle and with Islam as religion”, he will be forgiven. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 525)"
